    description: "Manage contacts from Instagram conversations in Linkar. Keep collected emails, useful answers, and conversation context ready for your team.",
    intro: "An enquiry is easier to help when its details stay together. Linkar’s contacts hold information gathered through supported Instagram conversations, including collected email addresses and configured field answers. That lets your team inspect the person’s request before responding. Organise around what the person actually shared; a contact record is conversation context, not permission to message indefinitely.",
    benefits: [["Find the relevant person", "Use the available contact search to locate an enquiry without scrolling through unrelated conversations. Clear, consistent collected fields make the result easier to use."], ["Keep answers readable", "Save project type, course interest, or timing where your flow asks for it. Use a field name the whole team understands rather than a campaign-specific abbreviation."], ["Prepare better follow-up", "Read the existing conversation before reaching out. A useful reply should respond to the stored enquiry and remain within the channel’s supported messaging rules."]],
    steps: [["Choose useful fields", "Collect the minimum details your team needs to help. Explain email collection and avoid sensitive or unnecessary questions in a public-facing intake journey."], ["Test a contact record", "Complete a flow using sample details and inspect the saved contact. Confirm the email and additional answers appear as expected and are attached to the right conversation."], ["Make review part of the work", "Decide how the team finds and responds to new enquiries. Keep records current and follow your privacy process for deletion or correction requests."]],
    example: { incoming: "I’m interested in the weekend course", reply: "Which email should we send the overview to?", next: "Keep the email and course interest together", note: "Sample contact information collected as part of a requested enquiry." },
    tip: ["A contact is context, not blanket consent", "Use collected details for the purpose you explained. If you want to enroll somebody in recurring marketing, obtain the appropriate permission through your chosen process. Do not infer that a saved Instagram contact can be messaged whenever you like. Keep the team’s workflow aligned with your published privacy and retention commitments."],
    faq: ["Does Linkar replace every CRM integration?", "Linkar keeps conversation contacts and the information collected by its flows. Any broader sales process or external CRM sync depends on your configured tools and supported connections. Check the specific workflow instead of assuming an automatic integration exists."],
